From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:17:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_hidspi_ts: Add the iPhone X touchscreen

The controller starts in its HBPP bootloader. The driver powers it
(analog supply, touch clock, reset), checks the bootloader with the NOP
probe and loads the firmware in SPI mode 3 by replaying the steps of
Apple's MTFW personality ("C1R1FC0,2"), which Orchard converts into an
op list: HBPP blobs and masked register writes acknowledged with 4bc1
and 4ad1, polls of a controller register, and the unit's calibrations
from the device tree. HBPP 0x105 answers a register read with 4c39, the
value and the sum of its bytes (iOS 0xfffffff0059216b8).

The firmware then speaks HIDSPI in mode 0, framed as in Asahi's
spi-hid-apple with 512-byte packets after 4 bytes of padding. It
announces its boot on device 0xd0 (a0 80 00 00), answers a get-report of
the surface descriptor 0xd9 (size in 0.01 mm and the sensor's edges),
and sends touches on interface 0 as report 0x44 with apple_z2's finger
records. Transfers keep the MTFW's 200 us CS-to-clock and 250 us
inter-transaction delays; without the latter the controller drops back
to its bootloader, which the driver then reloads.

Tested on the d221: the firmware loads on the first try, and touches
over the whole panel report at about 120 Hz.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig           |  12 +
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile          |   1 +
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_hidspi_ts.c | 735 ++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 748 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_hidspi_ts.c

